{"id":"n2-026","title":"Noun につき","romaji":"〜ni tsuki","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Indicates the reason, cause, or condition for something; 'due to', 'regarding', 'per'.","longExplanation":"The につき grammar point is used to express the reason, cause, or condition for an event or situation. In English, it can be translated as 'due to', 'regarding', 'per', or 'for each'. It can be used with nouns.","formation":"Noun + につき","examples":[{"jp":"試験につき、今日は静かにしてください。","romaji":"Shiken ni tsuki, kyou wa shizuka ni shite kudasai.","en":"Due to the exam, please be quiet today.","words":[{"surface":"試験","vocabId":"1312350","reading":"しけん"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"つき","vocabId":"1255430","reading":"つき","baseForm":"つく"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"今日","vocabId":"1579110","reading":"きょう"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"静か","vocabId":"1381820","reading":"しずか"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ください","vocabId":"1184270","reading":"ください","baseForm":"くださる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[1,2]},{"jp":"このエリアは工事中につき、通行止めです。","romaji":"Kono eria wa koujichuu ni tsuki, tsuukoudome desu.","en":"The area is closed for passage due to construction.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"エリア","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"工事","vocabId":"1278130","reading":"こうじ"},{"surface":"中","vocabId":"1423310","reading":"なか"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"つき","vocabId":"1255430","reading":"つき","baseForm":"つく"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"通行止め","vocabId":"1433190","reading":"つうこうどめ"},{"surface":"です","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[5,6]},{"jp":"博物館は整備中につき、入場料が無料です。","romaji":"Hakubutsukan wa seibichuu ni tsuki, nyuujouryou ga muryou desu.","en":"Due to maintenance, admission to the museum is free.","words":[{"surface":"博物館","